          "text": "Scrotal inspection"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left hemiscrotum enlarged and smooth, with non-erythematous, intact skin. Right testis normal size and lie."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Scrotal and testicular palpation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left-sided fluctuant, non-tender swelling superior and anterior to the testis. Left testis palpated posteriorly and feels normal in size and consistency; no discrete intratesticular solid mass. No warmth, epididymal or cord tenderness, or obvious cough impulse. Right testis normal in size, shape, and consistency and non-tender; right epididymis and cord normal. No inguinal lymph nodes."
      }
    },
